grainy-imgproc contains Rust implementations and source-derived ports of algorithms
and numerical conventions documented and implemented by the OpenCV project.
OpenCV is used only by the development-time Python golden generator; no OpenCV
binary or Python runtime is included in the Rust library.

Reference version: OpenCV 5.0.0 (public source tag, matching the installed oracle).
OpenCV 4.5.0 and later is distributed under Apache License 2.0. Some reference
files retain earlier BSD-style copyright notices. No C/C++ source files are
redistributed here. Grainy's original Rust code is covered by the workspace MIT
license. References inspected for algorithmic behavior:

Gaussian kernels / separable convolution / box filters / Sobel / median:
https://github.com/opencv/opencv/blob/5.0.0/modules/imgproc/src/smooth.dispatch.cpp
https://docs.opencv.org/4.x/d4/d86/group__imgproc__filter.html

Resize coordinates, area overlap/integer paths, and uint8 coefficient rounding:
https://github.com/opencv/opencv/blob/5.0.0/modules/imgproc/src/resize.cpp

Remap and affine/perspective transforms, including OpenCV 5 continuous kernels
and the retained fixed-point fallback:
https://github.com/opencv/opencv/blob/5.0.0/modules/imgproc/src/imgwarp.cpp
https://github.com/opencv/opencv/blob/5.0.0/modules/imgproc/src/warp_kernels.simd.hpp
https://github.com/opencv/opencv/blob/5.0.0/modules/imgproc/src/warp_common.scalar.hpp
https://github.com/opencv/opencv/blob/5.0.0/modules/imgproc/src/warp_common.vector.hpp

HSV/HLS scalar and SIMD arithmetic, hue sectors, uint8 tables:
https://github.com/opencv/opencv/blob/5.0.0/modules/imgproc/src/color_hsv.simd.hpp
https://docs.opencv.org/4.x/de/d25/imgproc_color_conversions.html

Morphological operations and structuring-element rasterization:
https://github.com/opencv/opencv/blob/5.0.0/modules/imgproc/src/morph.dispatch.cpp

Integral images and magnitude:
https://docs.opencv.org/4.x/d7/d1b/group__imgproc__misc.html
https://docs.opencv.org/4.x/d2/de8/group__core__array.html

